                  "startLine": 1392
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Knowledge review transitions are not atomic\n\nKnowledge review updates events sequentially and the run separately, leaving partial states on failure.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Race condition governance integrity\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-362\n\nRemediation:\nMove the entire transition into one locked database transaction.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Reject the negative path for knowledge-review-atomicity.\n- Preserve the intended bounded path.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Enforce the invariant in a shared database or admission control.\n- Add a negative regression test for the direct path."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:26f2b568b226e9c260744f1aa12909bbd1b7ecfc3ac466da5f89aa21fe1b42ff"
          },
